From de13f38147b7745b6645a1bc639006a9f046f143 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:27:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the non linear solver of PETSc (SNES)

The SNES entry of the factory of non linear solvers uses the non linear
solvers of PETSc through mfem::PetscNonlinearSolver, in parallel, per
problem (unlike the global mode of setPETSc): Newton's method with a
backtracking line search by default, and the other methods of SNES
selected by the options of PETSc (option Options, written with a prefix
which is unique to the resolution). The residual and the tangent
operator are the ones of the problem; the linear systems are solved by
the linear solver of the problem, seen by PETSc as a shell
preconditioner applied once (or preconditioning a Krylov solver of
PETSc), the tangent operator being a shell matrix (no copy, possibly
applied without assembly), or, with the option LinearSolver set to
PETSc, by the Krylov solvers and preconditioners of PETSc, the tangent
operator being converted to the AIJ format.

The functions called by PETSc do not throw: a failure of the integration
of the behaviours is reported as a domain error of the residual (the
backtracking line search reduces its step), a failure of the tangent
operator as a domain error of the Jacobian (checked, which only the
debug builds of PETSc do by default), and a failure of the linear solver
as a failure of the preconditioner, unless the failures of the linear
solver are discarded. SNES stops on the euclidean norm of the residual
relative to the reference norm, as the Newton solver, or when the
residual stagnates at the floor of the rounding errors; the behaviours
are integrated again at the solution if needed.

SNESSolverTest (two processes): Newton's method of SNES with and without
line search and its trust region method make the 9 iterations of the
Newton solver, with the same norms of the residual; the linear solver of
the problem preconditioning GMRES of PETSc, GMRES and GAMG of PETSc, and
the tangent operator applied without assembly give the same solution;
the linear solvers of PETSc are refused with the tangent operator
applied without assembly; the stagnation of the residual, the failures
of the integration and of the linear solver, the invalid options and the
sequential problems are checked.
